1
00:01:29,040 --> 00:01:30,200
I'm taking over.

2
00:01:30,280 --> 00:01:31,960
- What happened, Champ?
- Step back.

3
00:01:32,040 --> 00:01:33,320
Champ.

4
00:01:33,400 --> 00:01:35,040
Prepare for a disciplinary review.

5
00:01:42,080 --> 00:01:43,840
If I don't take down Peng today,

6
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:45,720
<i>you can step on my face.</i>

7
00:01:49,480 --> 00:01:52,120
<i>People in the territory</i>
<i>will start resisting.</i>

8
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:53,360
They'll want to break away,

9
00:01:53,440 --> 00:01:54,720
stop answering to anyone,

10
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:56,000
and stop paying their dues.

11
00:01:56,080 --> 00:01:57,880
You need to make them understand

12
00:01:57,960 --> 00:01:59,160
who they'll be paying from now on.

13
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:03,280
Without Boss Peng,
I don't answer to anyone.

14
00:02:03,360 --> 00:02:06,040
You two, get lost and tell your boss.

15
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:07,640
Wanna tell me yourself?

16
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:33,720
The brazen shooting at the boxing arena

17
00:02:33,800 --> 00:02:36,240
showed a complete disregard for the law.

18
00:02:36,840 --> 00:02:39,960
The authorities will crack down
on influential figures

19
00:02:40,040 --> 00:02:42,360
to protect the public

20
00:02:42,440 --> 00:02:43,400
<i>and carry out the policy of--</i>

21
00:02:44,480 --> 00:02:47,320
Crack down on influential figures?
Why not finish what you're saying?

22
00:02:47,400 --> 00:02:49,600
Who are the real influential figures here?

23
00:02:49,680 --> 00:02:53,240
Peng's case is bound to lead back to us.

24
00:02:53,880 --> 00:02:55,640
But there's no evidence we did it.

25
00:02:55,720 --> 00:02:58,320
Witnesses saw us shooting at them
at the boxing arena.

26
00:02:58,400 --> 00:02:59,680
So what?

27
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:01,640
It was chaos.

28
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:04,120
I was defending myself.
Everyone scattered.

29
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:07,360
We went our way, they went theirs,
then we met back at the boxing gym.

30
00:03:07,440 --> 00:03:09,520
Peng had enemies everywhere.

31
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:12,880
It could've been anyone
who lost out when Man lost.

32
00:03:15,680 --> 00:03:17,720
Either way, we need to be careful.

33
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:28,040
You've already summoned them in, right?

34
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:29,080
Yes, Sir.

35
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:32,120
If we can arrest them over this, do it.

36
00:03:32,720 --> 00:03:33,680
The drug case can wait.

37
00:03:34,280 --> 00:03:35,280
Yes.

38
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:38,520
But…

39
00:03:39,160 --> 00:03:40,200
But what?

40
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:46,640
I'll keep your valuables safe.

41
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:49,280
If anything happens, I'm counting on you.

42
00:03:54,480 --> 00:03:56,600
Good thing
you didn't get caught in the crossfire.

43
00:03:56,680 --> 00:03:58,040
Yeah.

44
00:03:59,480 --> 00:04:02,080
So why did you go
to the boxing arena that day?

45
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:07,360
I wanted to watch.

46
00:04:08,080 --> 00:04:09,160
Boxing?

47
00:04:09,880 --> 00:04:11,640
Why? Can't I?

48
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:16,680
I was just asking.

49
00:04:16,760 --> 00:04:18,560
Women usually aren't into boxing.

50
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:28,720
I'm off.
Let's get something good for lunch.

51
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:29,880
Yeah.

52
00:04:47,400 --> 00:04:50,000
Champ, did the chief
tell you to take over?

53
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:52,000
Yeah.

54
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:54,440
Why didn't you tell me?

55
00:05:02,560 --> 00:05:04,040
Me not telling you is understandable.

56
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:06,560
But you two,

57
00:05:07,320 --> 00:05:08,640
why didn't you say there'd be trouble?

58
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:11,640
I didn't know there'd be trouble.

59
00:05:12,360 --> 00:05:13,680
You didn't know,
or you're pretending you didn't?

60
00:05:14,280 --> 00:05:15,640
I really didn't know.

61
00:05:15,720 --> 00:05:17,360
Why would I put myself in danger if I did?

62
00:05:20,160 --> 00:05:21,120
You think I--

63
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:28,200
Hello.

64
00:05:40,560 --> 00:05:41,720
Of course, I remember you.

65
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:44,520
You found him?

66
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:02,600
I miss Dum.

67
00:06:04,560 --> 00:06:05,840
Yeah.

68
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:08,200
He's probably up there drinking
and swinging his legs.

69
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:21,080
I'm putting Dom in Dum's place.

70
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:23,720
I don't agree.

71
00:06:24,800 --> 00:06:25,880
Why not?

72
00:06:25,960 --> 00:06:29,240
The guys who've been here longer
might not like it.

73
00:06:33,320 --> 00:06:34,360
But I trust him.

74
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:35,880
I agree.

75
00:06:37,120 --> 00:06:39,280
It's not about who came first.

76
00:06:40,080 --> 00:06:41,960
It's about who you trust.

77
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:48,280
Trust someone too much, and you never know
when they'll turn on you.

78
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:52,200
- What are you trying to say?
- Hey.

79
00:06:52,280 --> 00:06:53,480
Enough.

80
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:55,120
That's enough.

81
00:06:56,440 --> 00:06:59,160
If you want power,
you need allies and friends on your side.

82
00:06:59,240 --> 00:07:01,000
Like I have you, Pong.

83
00:07:02,200 --> 00:07:04,720
I just want Dom to be your right-hand man

84
00:07:05,400 --> 00:07:06,720
and help you out.

85
00:07:11,160 --> 00:07:12,200
Trust me.

86
00:07:16,360 --> 00:07:19,200
- Here. Two iced coffees.
- Thanks, Ma'am.

87
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:20,240
Yeah.

88
00:07:20,320 --> 00:07:22,080
- How is it? Good?
- Whoa.

89
00:07:22,160 --> 00:07:23,960
- Why is it so…
- What?

90
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:26,360
It's good, right?

91
00:07:26,440 --> 00:07:27,720
- As good as ever.
- Yeah.

92
00:07:27,800 --> 00:07:30,160
That's more like it.

93
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:34,760
Bitter as hell. How did you make this?

94
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:40,240
Huh?

95
00:07:42,040 --> 00:07:43,680
Where did Oab and Pong go?

96
00:07:43,760 --> 00:07:47,560
No idea. Guess I'm not close enough
for them to tell me.

97
00:07:48,360 --> 00:07:50,320
That's just how Pong is. He trusts no one.

98
00:07:50,400 --> 00:07:51,280
You'll get used to it.

99
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:54,320
Why don't you guys work with me?

100
00:07:59,400 --> 00:08:00,600
Help me out.

101
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:08,280
Oab probably won't be at this much longer.

102
00:08:10,360 --> 00:08:12,120
And Pong doesn't like you.

103
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:17,920
A man without a boss
has a hard time surviving.

104
00:08:31,160 --> 00:08:33,799
Think it over and let me know soon.

105
00:08:38,960 --> 00:08:40,760
I think Liang has a point.

106
00:08:41,400 --> 00:08:42,440
About what?

107
00:08:42,520 --> 00:08:43,520
Hey.

108
00:08:44,120 --> 00:08:45,640
If Oab really steps away,

109
00:08:46,520 --> 00:08:47,760
Liang takes over Peng's territory,

110
00:08:48,520 --> 00:08:49,760
and Pong takes Oab's place.

111
00:08:50,600 --> 00:08:51,840
Where does that leave us?

112
00:08:55,640 --> 00:08:57,520
Pong doesn't like you.

113
00:08:58,400 --> 00:08:59,720
Liang's a good option.

114
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:10,240
They've summoned you.

115
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:11,640
Should I be worried?

116
00:09:16,680 --> 00:09:18,120
Why do you look so troubled?

117
00:09:22,800 --> 00:09:25,000
This summons
is probably just the beginning.

118
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:27,760
They're not trying to arrest you.

119
00:09:29,320 --> 00:09:30,360
They may want you dead.

120
00:09:32,040 --> 00:09:34,160
I must've gotten in the way
of their interests, huh?

121
00:09:34,760 --> 00:09:35,560
I think so.

122
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:38,720
So what do we do?

123
00:09:39,880 --> 00:09:42,280
I'm looking into who's backing them.

124
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:47,040
Could the same person be backing Peng too?

125
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:48,440
Probably.

126
00:09:49,520 --> 00:09:52,920
Peng's name has never appeared
on any of their arrest warrants.

127
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:55,920
So what should I tell them?

128
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:01,240
Say you acted in self-defense.

129
00:10:02,400 --> 00:10:05,280
Once you got away, you left.
You didn't go after them.

130
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:12,280
Won't you get in trouble too?

131
00:10:33,280 --> 00:10:35,640
POLICE SUSPENSION ORDER

132
00:10:35,720 --> 00:10:38,000
FOR SERIOUS MISCONDUCT WITHOUT JUST CAUSE,
THE OFFICER IS SUSPENDED FROM DUTY

133
00:10:48,800 --> 00:10:49,840
This was you, wasn't it?

134
00:10:54,040 --> 00:10:56,600
Am I in your way,
so you're trying to get rid of me?

135
00:11:06,680 --> 00:11:10,080
According to the order, you're suspended

136
00:11:10,160 --> 00:11:11,480
pending a disciplinary investigation.

137
00:11:11,560 --> 00:11:14,280
I know. I can read.

138
00:11:15,560 --> 00:11:17,560
I don't get the charge you pinned on me.

139
00:11:18,520 --> 00:11:19,520
You don't understand?

140
00:11:21,800 --> 00:11:24,160
It says you aided

141
00:11:24,240 --> 00:11:26,680
and abetted violent offenders.

142
00:11:26,760 --> 00:11:28,840
That's a criminal offense.

143
00:11:31,960 --> 00:11:33,040
I was doing my job.

144
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:37,480
Then explain yourself
to the committee investigating you,

145
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:39,600
not to me.

146
00:11:43,480 --> 00:11:46,080
I know you're behind this.

147
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:10,280
Pom.

148
00:12:12,440 --> 00:12:14,240
Is this about what happened at the arena?

149
00:12:18,080 --> 00:12:18,920
Don't talk here.

150
00:12:27,600 --> 00:12:30,560
If this is how things are,
I'll need your help.

151
00:12:32,160 --> 00:12:33,680
But that puts you at risk too.

152
00:12:36,040 --> 00:12:39,840
What's the point of clinging
to my position if the bad guys get ahead?

153
00:12:39,920 --> 00:12:41,080
I'd be ashamed to wear the badge.

154
00:12:43,600 --> 00:12:45,120
What can I do to help?

155
00:12:51,880 --> 00:12:55,000
Can you find out whose order this was?

156
00:13:00,920 --> 00:13:02,480
I want to know who Champ is working for.

157
00:13:02,560 --> 00:13:03,560
Sure.

158
00:13:05,520 --> 00:13:08,560
Fon, when they call Oab in
for questioning,

159
00:13:09,160 --> 00:13:10,520
could you sit in and listen?

160
00:13:15,880 --> 00:13:17,160
I don't know if I can.

161
00:13:17,760 --> 00:13:20,920
Here you go.

162
00:13:22,440 --> 00:13:23,320
Thank you.

163
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:37,760
Pong and Liang
can handle things outside for Oab.

164
00:13:39,160 --> 00:13:40,920
But if Oab gets locked up this time,

165
00:13:42,320 --> 00:13:43,840
I'm afraid he may never get out.

166
00:13:46,080 --> 00:13:47,840
And the real criminals will walk free.

167
00:13:51,720 --> 00:13:54,520
So they're determined
to put Oab behind bars?

168
00:13:55,400 --> 00:13:58,520
If any of Oab's men get arrested,
they probably won't make it out.

169
00:14:15,400 --> 00:14:16,960
Need another favor?

170
00:14:26,720 --> 00:14:30,000
Check who ordered this document for me.

171
00:14:33,360 --> 00:14:35,920
But keep it secret.

172
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:37,200
- Okay.
- Okay.

173
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:49,520
Have a drink,
and send us some customers too.

174
00:14:50,160 --> 00:14:52,400
- Haw. We're out of glasses.
- Huh?

175
00:14:52,480 --> 00:14:55,120
I'll go wash some in the back.
Watch the front for me.

176
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:31,040
It's almost healed.

177
00:15:32,440 --> 00:15:33,280
What is it, Fon?

178
00:15:36,840 --> 00:15:39,040
Champ wants us to meet him now.

179
00:15:40,160 --> 00:15:41,000
But…

180
00:15:42,560 --> 00:15:43,600
But what?

181
00:15:44,480 --> 00:15:48,520
I just found out from the prosecutor
that Champ handled the case of Arm,

182
00:15:48,600 --> 00:15:49,440
Oab's younger brother.

183
00:15:50,320 --> 00:15:52,440
He also handled
the case of the gunman killed

184
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:53,840
near the border.

185
00:15:54,560 --> 00:15:56,320
And in the case files,

186
00:15:56,400 --> 00:15:58,840
all the suspects' names were erased.

187
00:15:58,920 --> 00:16:02,000
Someone deliberately covered it all up
to protect Peng

188
00:16:02,800 --> 00:16:03,880
and whoever's behind him.

189
00:16:18,560 --> 00:16:21,520
Wow.

190
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:23,240
You came all the way here.

191
00:16:25,680 --> 00:16:27,120
Haw, where's Dom?

192
00:16:27,200 --> 00:16:28,960
He's out back.

193
00:16:33,800 --> 00:16:34,880
Dom.

194
00:16:36,080 --> 00:16:37,840
I don't think we should go.

195
00:16:38,520 --> 00:16:42,080
But if we don't,
Champ will know we've switched sides.

196
00:16:42,760 --> 00:16:44,120
Then he'll come after us.

197
00:16:46,120 --> 00:16:47,280
But if we go,

198
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:49,520
they might silence us.

199
00:17:37,960 --> 00:17:39,240
Took you long enough.

200
00:17:43,600 --> 00:17:44,560
Where's Dom?

201
00:17:45,160 --> 00:17:46,240
Oh.

202
00:17:46,320 --> 00:17:48,760
Oab called him over, so he couldn't come.

203
00:17:51,360 --> 00:17:54,240
I'd better go up alone. You wait here.

204
00:17:54,840 --> 00:17:56,640
If anything happens,
we can help each other.

205
00:18:41,320 --> 00:18:42,120
Hey.

206
00:18:43,200 --> 00:18:44,160
Sir.

207
00:18:45,120 --> 00:18:46,760
Your friends have all gone home.

208
00:19:00,840 --> 00:19:02,440
You should probably go back.

209
00:19:04,320 --> 00:19:05,720
You don't know, Haw?

210
00:19:06,520 --> 00:19:09,680
He didn't tell me.
He left all this for me to clean.

211
00:19:12,280 --> 00:19:14,240
I need to talk to him
about something important.

212
00:19:15,480 --> 00:19:16,600
Want me to pass on a message?

213
00:19:18,920 --> 00:19:20,040
No.

214
00:19:21,520 --> 00:19:23,400
Where can I find Dom?

215
00:19:42,040 --> 00:19:43,320
I'll be straight with you.

216
00:19:44,040 --> 00:19:45,360
If you betray me,

217
00:19:48,000 --> 00:19:49,600
I'll come after both of you.

218
00:19:59,680 --> 00:20:00,760
What do you want?

219
00:20:01,840 --> 00:20:03,640
I want you both to keep your mouths shut

220
00:20:04,200 --> 00:20:05,560
and do as I say.

221
00:20:08,520 --> 00:20:10,600
If Oab sees this stuff,

222
00:20:10,680 --> 00:20:13,040
you and Dom won't just be running from me.

223
00:20:14,280 --> 00:20:16,040
You'll be running for your lives
from him too.

224
00:20:16,120 --> 00:20:17,560
You already issued a warrant for him.

225
00:20:20,440 --> 00:20:24,720
If that were enough to take him down,
I wouldn't need Dom inside his crew.

226
00:20:25,880 --> 00:20:27,360
What did he ever do to you?

227
00:20:29,240 --> 00:20:31,120
He got involved where he shouldn't,

228
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:35,600
helped people he shouldn't,
and did things he shouldn't.

229
00:20:46,680 --> 00:20:49,880
Tell Dom not to make this difficult.

230
00:20:51,280 --> 00:20:54,520
Whatever you two do, I know about it.

231
00:21:28,840 --> 00:21:29,480
Hey!

232
00:21:55,320 --> 00:21:56,200
Fon.

233
00:21:56,280 --> 00:21:57,640
Dom.

234
00:21:58,160 --> 00:21:59,480
Watch out!

235
00:22:06,840 --> 00:22:09,240
I'm gonna get you!

236
00:22:09,320 --> 00:22:10,480
Take this!

237
00:23:54,720 --> 00:23:56,600
- Dom.
- Shit!

238
00:23:57,160 --> 00:23:58,880
Damn.

239
00:23:58,960 --> 00:24:01,240
- Why are the lights off?
- I'm saving electricity.

240
00:24:01,960 --> 00:24:03,320
- Geez.
- Where've you been?

241
00:24:03,400 --> 00:24:05,280
- Why do you care?
- Hey.

242
00:24:05,360 --> 00:24:07,720
Plern waited for you at the bar
until closing.

243
00:24:08,600 --> 00:24:09,880
So what?

244
00:24:09,960 --> 00:24:11,040
Whoa!

245
00:24:11,760 --> 00:24:12,880
Hey!

246
00:24:12,960 --> 00:24:14,280
What happened to you?

247
00:24:16,160 --> 00:24:17,360
Some guys jumped me.

248
00:24:17,440 --> 00:24:18,600
Go see a doctor.

249
00:24:18,680 --> 00:24:20,200
I'm not going. I'm fine.

250
00:24:20,280 --> 00:24:22,280
Fine? You're covered in blood.

251
00:24:22,360 --> 00:24:23,960
- It's nothing.
- You look like you've been to war. No!

252
00:24:24,040 --> 00:24:24,960
Go see a doctor.

253
00:24:26,400 --> 00:24:28,320
Wait here a second.

254
00:24:28,840 --> 00:24:31,880
Yeah. Sure, got it.

255
00:24:31,960 --> 00:24:33,000
Those bastards are at it again.

256
00:24:33,960 --> 00:24:36,080
Wake the guys up and go help him.

257
00:24:36,680 --> 00:24:38,520
- Let's go.
- Go.

258
00:24:39,680 --> 00:24:41,480
This is the fifth place.

259
00:24:41,560 --> 00:24:43,360
What the hell's gotten into them?

260
00:24:47,480 --> 00:24:48,840
They're coming.

261
00:24:50,600 --> 00:24:51,920
Peng's gone.

262
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:53,720
I run this territory now.

263
00:24:54,760 --> 00:24:57,080
From now on, you pay your protection money

264
00:24:57,160 --> 00:24:58,840
to me and no one else.

265
00:25:02,200 --> 00:25:03,720
If I pay you,

266
00:25:05,160 --> 00:25:07,120
I won't be able to sell my stuff.

267
00:25:07,200 --> 00:25:09,520
Keep doing whatever you were doing.
I won't interfere.

268
00:25:11,000 --> 00:25:13,360
But from now on,
Liang will look after you.

269
00:25:15,360 --> 00:25:16,680
So there won't be any problems.

270
00:25:32,320 --> 00:25:33,760
You don't want trouble, do you?

271
00:25:38,680 --> 00:25:40,400
I'm just trying to make a living.

272
00:25:42,480 --> 00:25:44,080
Why would I want trouble?

273
00:25:44,160 --> 00:25:46,280
Then why won't you pay me?

274
00:25:50,400 --> 00:25:51,840
They want what you have.

275
00:25:58,640 --> 00:25:59,720
Who?

276
00:26:06,000 --> 00:26:07,520
The one giving the orders.

277
00:26:10,840 --> 00:26:12,480
You know you can trust me.

278
00:26:13,720 --> 00:26:14,760
Tell me who it is,

279
00:26:14,840 --> 00:26:16,280
and I guarantee you'll be safe.

280
00:26:35,880 --> 00:26:37,080
Oab.

281
00:27:04,760 --> 00:27:06,280
Good thing you got there in time.

282
00:27:06,360 --> 00:27:07,800
Otherwise, I'd be dead.

283
00:27:07,880 --> 00:27:09,200
Yes.

284
00:27:11,440 --> 00:27:12,680
Oab.

285
00:27:15,240 --> 00:27:17,120
I think I'll work with Liang.

286
00:27:22,080 --> 00:27:23,680
Why aren't you staying with Pong?

287
00:27:24,520 --> 00:27:26,000
It seems like Pong

288
00:27:26,920 --> 00:27:27,920
doesn't want me around.

289
00:27:29,280 --> 00:27:31,320
I think it's better to work
with someone who's comfortable

290
00:27:31,400 --> 00:27:32,720
having me around.

291
00:27:36,320 --> 00:27:37,560
Yeah.

292
00:27:46,640 --> 00:27:47,680
Hey, Oab.

293
00:27:49,880 --> 00:27:52,160
- What happened?
- What are you doing here?

294
00:27:53,720 --> 00:27:55,520
I'm free now. I got suspended.

295
00:27:56,360 --> 00:27:57,200
I've got nothing to do.

296
00:28:00,480 --> 00:28:02,520
I'm fine now. But you…

297
00:28:03,160 --> 00:28:05,360
Keep coming to see me
and you could get disciplined.

298
00:28:05,440 --> 00:28:09,080
You want me to stop seeing you?
We're friends.

299
00:28:09,680 --> 00:28:11,240
There's nothing in it for us.

300
00:28:14,960 --> 00:28:16,040
Oab.

301
00:28:20,360 --> 00:28:21,760
The boss wants to see you.

302
00:28:29,040 --> 00:28:30,400
Hello, Sir.

303
00:28:34,280 --> 00:28:37,080
Wait outside.
The less you know, the better.

304
00:28:41,360 --> 00:28:42,960
- Sit down.
- Yes, Sir.

305
00:28:46,640 --> 00:28:48,160
He wants to know

306
00:28:48,240 --> 00:28:51,680
what you'll do with the extra money
collected from Peng's territory.

307
00:28:53,800 --> 00:28:54,840
Well.

308
00:28:55,960 --> 00:28:57,880
I'll send it to him through you,
like before.

309
00:28:57,960 --> 00:28:59,960
The one receiving it isn't the problem.

310
00:29:00,760 --> 00:29:02,880
The one who used to get a cut
and doesn't anymore

311
00:29:03,480 --> 00:29:04,520
could cause trouble for us.

312
00:29:07,080 --> 00:29:10,840
You've been summoned
as a suspect in Peng's murder.

313
00:29:11,480 --> 00:29:12,320
You know that?

314
00:29:13,520 --> 00:29:14,840
Yes, Sir.

315
00:29:17,760 --> 00:29:19,560
If I hadn't done it,
he would've killed me.

316
00:29:20,160 --> 00:29:22,480
- Did you clean everything up?
- All taken care of.

317
00:29:24,080 --> 00:29:27,040
Alright. I'll talk to him

318
00:29:27,120 --> 00:29:29,680
and see what can be done
about the summons.

319
00:29:30,280 --> 00:29:32,040
Maybe we can make things easier for you.

320
00:29:32,640 --> 00:29:33,600
Thank you, Sir.

321
00:29:36,160 --> 00:29:37,600
There's one more thing.

322
00:29:54,120 --> 00:29:55,920
The money for the village project.

323
00:29:57,280 --> 00:29:59,280
But Plern hasn't even gone
to inspect the site yet.

324
00:29:59,360 --> 00:30:01,160
She said she'll pay the money

325
00:30:02,320 --> 00:30:03,560
in exchange for Dom.

326
00:30:13,680 --> 00:30:15,560
Did he help you with the summons or not?

327
00:30:17,960 --> 00:30:20,520
Huh? Then why are you so stressed?

328
00:30:23,000 --> 00:30:25,800
Money can buy anything.

329
00:30:27,560 --> 00:30:28,880
It buys people.

330
00:30:30,200 --> 00:30:31,560
Even their dignity.

331
00:30:35,720 --> 00:30:37,280
But it can't buy everyone.

332
00:30:40,880 --> 00:30:44,240
The people who want me dead can't touch me
because my money reaches them.

333
00:30:45,280 --> 00:30:46,960
Think about it. If one day I quit

334
00:30:47,880 --> 00:30:50,720
and can't make money for them anymore,
do you think I'll still survive?

335
00:31:01,120 --> 00:31:03,640
Once you're in this deep,
it's hard to get out.

336
00:31:06,600 --> 00:31:08,800
When that day comes,
I can't protect the people I love.

337
00:31:23,520 --> 00:31:24,640
But if you really want out,

338
00:31:26,120 --> 00:31:27,440
there is a way.

339
00:33:32,440 --> 00:33:33,520
Just got back?

340
00:33:36,760 --> 00:33:38,480
I've been back for a while.

341
00:33:42,040 --> 00:33:44,160
I'm moving back to the police flats.

342
00:33:47,760 --> 00:33:48,640
When?

343
00:33:49,960 --> 00:33:52,840
Either this weekend or next.

344
00:33:54,600 --> 00:33:56,640
Fon, the flat's tiny.
Will you be comfortable there?

345
00:33:58,440 --> 00:33:59,440
Oab.

346
00:34:11,320 --> 00:34:12,600
When you're ready, let me know.

347
00:34:13,920 --> 00:34:15,239
I'll help you move.

348
00:34:20,400 --> 00:34:21,719
Thank you.

349
00:35:33,240 --> 00:35:34,520
I want to ask you something.

350
00:35:35,720 --> 00:35:37,040
Yes?

351
00:35:40,920 --> 00:35:42,240
Do you want out?

352
00:35:44,120 --> 00:35:47,080
Out? Out of what?

353
00:35:47,160 --> 00:35:49,120
Quit what you're doing.

354
00:35:49,200 --> 00:35:51,360
Live an easy life.

355
00:35:52,480 --> 00:35:53,880
Have plenty of money.

356
00:35:56,440 --> 00:35:57,800
What's going on?

357
00:35:59,040 --> 00:36:00,560
Mr. Pinit, Plern's father,

358
00:36:01,640 --> 00:36:04,040
offered money to buy you out.

359
00:36:23,120 --> 00:36:24,000
Where's Miss Plern?

360
00:36:24,080 --> 00:36:25,040
Probably in the garden.

361
00:36:27,360 --> 00:36:28,800
Do you think I'm some kept man?

362
00:36:30,920 --> 00:36:31,920
Where should we go today?

363
00:36:32,000 --> 00:36:34,640
I asked if you think I'm some kept man.

364
00:36:38,480 --> 00:36:39,520
No.

365
00:36:40,760 --> 00:36:42,240
But you're trying to buy me.

366
00:36:46,120 --> 00:36:48,400
Why do you keep risking your life?

367
00:36:49,680 --> 00:36:51,800
Aren't you afraid
of getting hurt or killed?

368
00:36:51,880 --> 00:36:53,320
That's my business.

369
00:36:54,040 --> 00:36:55,360
But I'm scared.

370
00:36:58,240 --> 00:37:01,160
I'm scared you'll get hurt.
I'm scared you'll die.

371
00:37:02,440 --> 00:37:05,360
That's why I asked Dad to invest in Oab,

372
00:37:06,960 --> 00:37:08,440
in exchange for your life.

373
00:37:13,040 --> 00:37:14,920
Even though you know I don't love you?

374
00:37:19,200 --> 00:37:20,200
Yes.

375
00:37:23,600 --> 00:37:26,000
Why keep risking your life for nothing?

376
00:37:29,440 --> 00:37:32,160
If your life means nothing to you,

377
00:37:33,400 --> 00:37:35,080
then sell it to me.

378
00:37:37,560 --> 00:37:42,040
Because your life matters to me.

379
00:38:41,320 --> 00:38:42,640
Champ still hasn't come in?

380
00:38:45,160 --> 00:38:46,120
Not yet.

381
00:38:47,000 --> 00:38:48,520
He's probably busy outside.

382
00:39:00,800 --> 00:39:03,000
I found what you asked me to look into.

383
00:39:06,600 --> 00:39:07,400
You did?

384
00:39:07,480 --> 00:39:11,520
Wow, now you're suddenly interested in me.

385
00:39:12,720 --> 00:39:13,840
By the way,

386
00:39:14,440 --> 00:39:16,120
why do you want to know
who gave the order?

387
00:39:16,840 --> 00:39:19,520
Well, I've been following this
from the start.

388
00:39:21,640 --> 00:39:22,720
True.

389
00:39:24,680 --> 00:39:25,520
Come on, tell me.

390
00:39:29,840 --> 00:39:31,000
Buy me dinner.

391
00:39:31,080 --> 00:39:32,120
Yeah.

392
00:39:34,120 --> 00:39:36,800
- And dessert.
- Fine.

393
00:39:36,880 --> 00:39:38,240
Just tell me who ordered it.

394
00:39:42,520 --> 00:39:43,760
Chief Saen.

395
00:39:51,200 --> 00:39:53,560
Huh? What's wrong?

396
00:39:54,760 --> 00:39:56,600
That's normal, isn't it?

397
00:39:56,680 --> 00:39:58,560
Champ works for Chief Saen.

398
00:39:58,640 --> 00:40:00,680
Of course his boss would give the order.

399
00:40:03,160 --> 00:40:04,160
Yeah.

400
00:40:04,680 --> 00:40:07,480
I thought it might be someone else.

401
00:40:53,800 --> 00:40:54,640
Fon.

402
00:40:57,600 --> 00:40:59,800
Dom, did Oab send you to pick me up?

403
00:41:16,840 --> 00:41:18,640
Do you think my life matters?

404
00:41:20,920 --> 00:41:21,760
Of course.

405
00:41:22,600 --> 00:41:24,160
It matters a lot.

406
00:41:25,840 --> 00:41:27,200
What's wrong?

407
00:41:37,960 --> 00:41:39,960
When will all this finally end?

408
00:41:48,120 --> 00:41:49,480
If we quit, it's dangerous.

409
00:41:52,680 --> 00:41:54,480
If we stay, we risk getting killed.

410
00:41:58,160 --> 00:41:59,520
And if we don't make it,

411
00:42:00,880 --> 00:42:02,720
we won't get to be together anyway.

412
00:42:17,200 --> 00:42:19,080
Excuse me, this is my parking spot.

413
00:42:21,360 --> 00:42:22,840
Okay, I'll move my car.

414
00:42:23,800 --> 00:42:24,800
Thank you.

415
00:42:38,480 --> 00:42:39,800
Hey.

416
00:42:39,880 --> 00:42:42,440
Come help me set up the chairs.

417
00:42:42,520 --> 00:42:43,280
Yeah.

418
00:42:44,880 --> 00:42:46,200
Where've you been? Why are you late?

419
00:42:46,800 --> 00:42:47,760
I was getting my helmet fixed.

420
00:42:47,840 --> 00:42:49,160
Oh.

421
00:42:51,840 --> 00:42:54,080
- I'm only ten minutes late.
- Hey.

422
00:42:54,160 --> 00:42:55,880
Late is late.

423
00:42:56,440 --> 00:42:57,560
Even one minute is late.

424
00:42:57,640 --> 00:42:59,600
Fine. I'll make up for it, okay?

425
00:43:00,280 --> 00:43:02,040
Hey, I'm just messing with you.

426
00:43:02,120 --> 00:43:03,520
I wanted to know where you were.

427
00:43:06,240 --> 00:43:08,200
One whiskey and some ice, please.

428
00:43:14,000 --> 00:43:15,240
You, honestly.

429
00:43:29,200 --> 00:43:30,320
- Dom.
- Yeah?

430
00:43:30,400 --> 00:43:32,160
You handle the front.

431
00:43:32,840 --> 00:43:33,800
I'll take care of the back.

432
00:43:37,360 --> 00:43:38,440
- Thank you.
- Sure.

433
00:43:53,000 --> 00:43:54,560
Are you sure about this?

434
00:43:56,400 --> 00:43:57,960
It's a bar.

435
00:43:58,040 --> 00:43:59,680
Anyone can come in, right?

436
00:44:00,440 --> 00:44:02,680
I'm just a customer.

437
00:44:07,160 --> 00:44:08,680
You do your job.

438
00:44:08,760 --> 00:44:10,560
We don't even have to talk.

439
00:44:12,000 --> 00:44:14,080
I just wanted to be here and support you.

440
00:44:57,440 --> 00:44:58,600
One bottle of whiskey for table two.

441
00:45:04,720 --> 00:45:05,840
- Dom.
- Huh?

442
00:45:06,960 --> 00:45:09,440
I think you should tell her to go home.

443
00:45:09,520 --> 00:45:10,640
Oab might see her.

444
00:45:14,560 --> 00:45:15,520
There he is.

445
00:45:23,400 --> 00:45:25,120
- What'll you have?
- The usual.

446
00:45:25,200 --> 00:45:26,760
Why are you drinking here alone?

447
00:45:27,960 --> 00:45:28,840
You?

448
00:45:31,200 --> 00:45:32,600
I don't feel like going home yet.

449
00:45:34,480 --> 00:45:36,080
Don't want to see me?

450
00:45:37,440 --> 00:45:38,760
I just wanted to hang out.

451
00:45:39,520 --> 00:45:41,360
I thought this would be the safest place.

452
00:45:48,240 --> 00:45:49,520
Want to go home together tonight?

453
00:45:51,360 --> 00:45:52,600
Okay.

454
00:45:55,720 --> 00:45:56,840
Dom.

455
00:46:07,520 --> 00:46:08,680
Have you decided about Plern?

456
00:46:11,400 --> 00:46:12,320
I'm not quitting.

457
00:46:13,320 --> 00:46:14,120
Why not?

458
00:46:15,440 --> 00:46:16,680
I want to be like you.

459
00:46:18,240 --> 00:46:21,040
Have money and power.

460
00:46:24,320 --> 00:46:28,080
You want to be like me,
but I want to be like you.

461
00:46:29,400 --> 00:46:32,560
If someone gave me an opportunity
like that, I wouldn't think twice.

462
00:46:36,800 --> 00:46:38,920
I don't want to be someone money can buy.

463
00:46:47,240 --> 00:46:49,040
Liang's going to pick up
the goods tonight.

464
00:46:50,920 --> 00:46:52,320
If you're working with him,

465
00:46:53,480 --> 00:46:54,800
you have to go with him.

466
00:46:56,600 --> 00:46:57,800
Okay.

467
00:47:09,520 --> 00:47:10,640
Hey.

468
00:47:17,880 --> 00:47:20,240
You won't regret choosing me. Let's go.

469
00:47:31,040 --> 00:47:33,200
Never thought Dom would come this far.

470
00:47:35,960 --> 00:47:39,720
He's nothing like that temple-fair boxer
I watched back then.

471
00:47:56,280 --> 00:47:58,040
Boss, one black coffee.

472
00:48:00,720 --> 00:48:02,000
What's all this?

473
00:48:02,080 --> 00:48:03,120
Look at you.

474
00:48:03,920 --> 00:48:05,400
Since you got suspended,

475
00:48:05,480 --> 00:48:06,880
you've got plenty of time for me.

476
00:48:06,960 --> 00:48:07,800
Hey.

477
00:48:08,440 --> 00:48:09,880
I'm making time to come see you guys.

478
00:48:11,200 --> 00:48:12,600
Taking time out from your naps?

479
00:48:13,760 --> 00:48:14,880
Screw you, Pong.

480
00:48:16,200 --> 00:48:17,800
I'm busier now than when I was on duty.

481
00:48:19,360 --> 00:48:21,240
Last time you said you weren't busy.

482
00:48:21,320 --> 00:48:22,520
What are you so busy with now?

483
00:48:23,320 --> 00:48:24,960
Getting myself into trouble.

484
00:48:29,040 --> 00:48:30,000
Hey.

485
00:48:31,280 --> 00:48:34,160
Someone ordered
the people in Peng's territory to defy me.

486
00:48:35,400 --> 00:48:37,040
The bar owner
was about to tell me who it was,

487
00:48:38,320 --> 00:48:40,200
but their man shot him first.

488
00:48:42,880 --> 00:48:44,680
That's what I came to tell you.

489
00:48:45,280 --> 00:48:46,760
You're up against someone powerful.

490
00:48:47,360 --> 00:48:51,440
I'm looking into
who ordered the hit on you at the arena.

491
00:48:52,040 --> 00:48:52,840
Wasn't it Peng?

492
00:48:55,560 --> 00:48:57,320
I think Peng was just working for them.

493
00:49:04,800 --> 00:49:08,200
Champ, the guy in the same division
as your girlfriend Fon.

494
00:49:09,640 --> 00:49:12,200
The one who took over at the boxing arena?

495
00:49:13,080 --> 00:49:14,520
Yeah.

496
00:49:14,600 --> 00:49:16,320
Something feels off.

497
00:49:16,400 --> 00:49:19,080
It was only a few hours of security duty.

498
00:49:19,160 --> 00:49:21,240
Why would the chief
send someone to replace you?

499
00:49:22,600 --> 00:49:24,000
I've been suspicious since that day.

500
00:49:24,640 --> 00:49:25,880
What did you find?

501
00:49:27,600 --> 00:49:30,080
Yeah. I found out he's taking money.

502
00:49:30,160 --> 00:49:31,080
A lot of it.

503
00:49:33,080 --> 00:49:34,120
From who?

504
00:49:35,360 --> 00:49:36,400
I don't know.

505
00:49:37,480 --> 00:49:40,280
But if I keep digging,
I'm sure I'll find out

506
00:49:40,360 --> 00:49:42,080
who's paying him

507
00:49:43,080 --> 00:49:45,640
and, more importantly,
who he passes the money to.

508
00:49:47,080 --> 00:49:48,800
Probably whoever wants me dead.

509
00:49:49,320 --> 00:49:52,280
Could be. Champ handled Arm's case.

510
00:49:53,080 --> 00:49:55,440
It never got solved
because they couldn't catch the killer.

511
00:49:55,520 --> 00:49:57,600
Or maybe someone ordered him not to.

512
00:50:12,800 --> 00:50:13,840
Thanks.

513
00:50:16,520 --> 00:50:18,360
Is there still news
about the boxing arena?

514
00:50:18,440 --> 00:50:21,040
Some, but it's died down.

515
00:50:22,320 --> 00:50:23,240
Liang.

516
00:50:23,320 --> 00:50:25,040
Can I work with you too?

517
00:50:33,200 --> 00:50:35,200
Aren't you afraid
Pong will come after you?

518
00:50:36,800 --> 00:50:40,440
Dom and I are close.
If he's with you, I want to be with him.

519
00:50:42,600 --> 00:50:43,480
Yeah.

520
00:50:44,120 --> 00:50:45,120
Thanks.

521
00:50:45,880 --> 00:50:47,040
I'll talk to Oab about it.

522
00:50:51,560 --> 00:50:53,960
Hey, if you keep buying drugs
in small amounts,

523
00:50:54,840 --> 00:50:55,920
how will you ever get rich?

524
00:50:56,000 --> 00:50:57,680
One step at a time.

525
00:51:01,640 --> 00:51:02,960
Were you doing this

526
00:51:03,640 --> 00:51:05,080
behind Peng's back too?

527
00:51:06,480 --> 00:51:07,720
You ask too many questions.

528
00:51:12,520 --> 00:51:14,240
Why don't you talk to Oab?

529
00:51:15,680 --> 00:51:19,480
Ask him for some money
and buy a big batch.

530
00:51:29,160 --> 00:51:30,360
Why didn't you stop Pom?

531
00:51:33,200 --> 00:51:35,800
- I think it's too risky.
- Would he listen if I tried?

532
00:51:39,040 --> 00:51:40,600
I'm worried they'll come after him too.

533
00:51:48,800 --> 00:51:49,640
What is it?

534
00:51:54,240 --> 00:51:55,280
I need to discuss something.

535
00:52:17,600 --> 00:52:18,920
Why don't you go in and talk with them?

536
00:52:20,680 --> 00:52:21,760
Here we go.

537
00:52:25,920 --> 00:52:27,920
You'd rather work with Liang than me, huh?

538
00:52:31,320 --> 00:52:34,360
Fine. You two are a perfect match.

539
00:52:35,720 --> 00:52:36,840
You're both traitors.

540
00:52:39,040 --> 00:52:40,360
You two are done.

541
00:52:43,040 --> 00:52:45,480
Whoever we work with,
we're still working for Oab, right?

542
00:52:49,520 --> 00:52:51,360
If you didn't dislike us,

543
00:52:51,880 --> 00:52:53,960
I'd actually want to work with you.

544
00:53:12,000 --> 00:53:13,240
I'm gonna get back to work.

545
00:53:26,280 --> 00:53:27,240
I can fund you.

546
00:53:30,600 --> 00:53:31,600
But I want something in return.

547
00:53:34,680 --> 00:53:36,640
I want Peng's secret ledger.

548
00:53:49,040 --> 00:53:50,440
He usually kept it himself.

549
00:53:51,680 --> 00:53:52,640
I'll have to find it.

550
00:53:52,720 --> 00:53:54,440
That's what I'm asking you to do.

551
00:53:55,520 --> 00:53:56,480
I want it.

552
00:54:10,040 --> 00:54:11,080
Nothing, Liang.

553
00:54:11,680 --> 00:54:13,440
I've seen him put it
in that drawer before.

554
00:54:14,200 --> 00:54:15,680
None of these are it.

555
00:54:17,160 --> 00:54:19,120
Could someone have moved it?

556
00:54:19,200 --> 00:54:20,800
I doubt anyone could have.

557
00:54:20,880 --> 00:54:23,320
We're the first ones
to come in here since he died.

558
00:54:29,560 --> 00:54:30,720
Liang.

559
00:54:33,760 --> 00:54:35,120
I found something.

560
00:54:41,000 --> 00:54:42,680
Why does he want it?

561
00:54:43,440 --> 00:54:45,280
To protect himself.

562
00:54:46,320 --> 00:54:47,240
From who?

563
00:54:47,320 --> 00:54:51,400
The secret ledger
lists everyone taking our money.

564
00:54:51,480 --> 00:54:55,560
It also contains evidence
proving they really took the money.

565
00:54:56,080 --> 00:54:57,880
People like us who pay them

566
00:54:58,920 --> 00:55:00,000
need some leverage

567
00:55:00,080 --> 00:55:02,440
in case they don't keep their word.

568
00:55:04,200 --> 00:55:06,680
So every powerful figure
keeps something like this?

569
00:55:07,760 --> 00:55:08,920
I don't know.

570
00:55:09,680 --> 00:55:12,160
But everyone wants some protection

571
00:55:12,240 --> 00:55:13,920
against being betrayed, right?

572
00:55:37,680 --> 00:55:39,080
Haw.

573
00:55:39,640 --> 00:55:40,760
Yeah?

574
00:55:40,840 --> 00:55:44,240
You really think
Oab wants Peng's secret ledger

575
00:55:44,320 --> 00:55:45,960
just to protect himself?

576
00:55:48,000 --> 00:55:50,560
I don't know. I'm sleepy.

577
00:55:50,640 --> 00:55:53,040
I bet Oab has one of his own too.

578
00:55:54,400 --> 00:55:57,120
Maybe. I don't know.

579
00:55:58,720 --> 00:56:01,120
And he wants Peng's ledger

580
00:56:02,600 --> 00:56:05,960
because it lists everyone Peng paid.

581
00:56:06,840 --> 00:56:10,040
I bet whoever was backing Peng
is in there too.

582
00:56:21,760 --> 00:56:26,720
PROTECTION PAYMENTS, AUGUST 1991

583
00:56:41,600 --> 00:56:44,000
Go back and find Oab's secret ledger.

584
00:56:44,640 --> 00:56:45,760
If you still can't find it,

585
00:56:45,840 --> 00:56:47,200
don't leave until you do.

586
00:56:47,280 --> 00:56:50,040
Don't forget what I'm capable of.

587
00:56:52,120 --> 00:56:53,240
How could it disappear?

588
00:56:57,760 --> 00:56:59,480
Are you trying to betray me?

589
00:56:59,560 --> 00:57:02,240
Freedom is damn precious.

590
00:57:02,320 --> 00:57:03,600
Oab came in on the summons, Sir.

591
00:57:04,200 --> 00:57:06,120
- Where is he?
- In the interrogation room.

592
00:57:13,920 --> 00:57:15,440
The only way we can get out

593
00:57:15,520 --> 00:57:18,480
is to make sure Oab
never gets out of prison.

594
00:57:22,120 --> 00:57:23,880
‪BOSS WUT (BANGKOK), BOSS FHAI (BANGKOK),
‪BOSS PHAO (KANCHANABURI)

595
00:57:23,960 --> 00:57:24,840
‪BOSS PLA (SUPHANBURI),
‪BOSS PRAKIT (BANGKOK)

596
00:58:01,160 --> 00:58:03,120
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
